## SavedVariables: GearSweepDB

## X-ReleaseNotes: Sweeps your bags, bank and Warband Bank for gear to disenchant or wear. Disenchant mode filters for Uncommon/Rare/Epic equipment that's Adventurer-tier and/or from a previous season, ignoring non-gear whites like shirts and tabards, with independent toggles for quality, slot, item level range, and Adventurer-tier/previous-season inclusion. Upgrade mode instead filters for equipment your character can actually use - checked against class/armor/weapon proficiency and Blizzard's own "Best in Slot" spec-relevance signal - that's also a genuine item-level upgrade over what's currently equipped (or your average equipped item level, for a slot that's never been filled), then pre-checks the single highest-item-level candidate per slot (top two for dual-slot rings/trinkets; two-hand weapons and one-hand+offhand pairs are scored as a pair so both never get pre-checked together - whichever has the higher average item level wins). "Pull Selected" moves every checked item into your bags; GearSweep never disenchants or sells anything on its own. The sweep window opens automatically when you visit your bank or Warband Bank (toggle with /gs autoopen or the options panel). Configure under Options > AddOns > GearSweep or with /gs (alias /gearsweep); /gs options opens the settings panel, /gs debug turns on diagnostic logging (plus slots/upgrades/weapons/item <name> sub-dumps), /gs status shows current settings, and /gs help lists every command. Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/GearSweep

